  <data name="Export" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation exports all versions of each title to the specifed folder. Each file will be named in accordance with the date it was written, its title, language and version / revision. Only files that have changed or are not present in the export directory will be exported. Extra files in the export directory will be deleted.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExportFileFormat" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This folder contains exported versions of each title tracked by {0}.
Files are named according to the date they were first written, title, version, and language.

Usually, the individual files are kept in different sub directories; this directory has all files in one place.

Last exported: {1}</value>
    <comment>Text that is written to the export read me.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation renames the files that are used for external submission messages to correspond to the date / time of the message and the message subject.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Orphan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation searches all files beneath the title root directory to find those files that are not associated with a title entry. The submission document folder and title export folder are automatically excluded from the search if they exist beneath title root. You can exclude other folders in configuration.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubmissionMetadata" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation verifies that all submission documents are present on disk and updates meta data that is stored in the database regarding each file, such as the last updated date/time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleList" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation creates a text file that has a list of all titles and their corresponding versions.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleMetadata" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This operation verifies that all files associated with title versions are present on disk and updates meta data that is stored in the database regarding each file, such as last updated date/time and word count.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="VersionProperties" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>These properties are the same ones you can change from within Microsoft Word; they are saved within the document itself.

When you save properties here however, the document's file  modification date is not set to the current date / time as it is when you make the changes from within Word. Instead,  the modification date is incremented by 15 seconds from its original.</value>
